{start_of_verse label="Verse 1"}
When [Am]Johnny comes marching home again,
Hurrah! Hur[C]rah!
We'll [Am]give him a hearty welcome then,
Hurrah! Hur[E]rah!
The [Am]men will cheer and the [C]boys will shout,
The [G]ladies they will [E]all turn out,
And we'll [Am]all feel [C]gay
When [E]Johnny comes marching [Am]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 2"}
The [Am]old church bell will peal with joy,
Hurrah! Hur[C]rah!
To [Am]welcome home our darling boy,
Hurrah! Hur[E]rah!
The [Am]village lads and [C]lasses say
With [G]roses they will [E]strew the way,
And we'll [Am]all feel [C]gay
When [E]Johnny comes marching [Am]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 3"}
Get [Am]ready for the Jubilee,
Hurrah! Hur[C]rah!
We'll [Am]give the hero three times three,
Hurrah! Hur[E]rah!
The [Am]laurel wreath is [C]ready now
To [G]place upon his [E]loyal brow,
And we'll [Am]all feel [C]gay
When [E]Johnny comes marching [Am]home.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse label="Verse 4"}
Let [Am]love and friendship on that day,
Hurrah! Hur[C]rah!
Their [Am]choicest treasures then display,
Hurrah! Hur[E]rah!
And [Am]let each one per[C]form some part,
To [G]fill with joy the [E]warrior's heart,
And we'll [Am]all feel [C]gay
When [E]Johnny comes marching [Am]home.
{end_of_verse}
{x_end: Am}
